NAME
    break - exit the nearest enclosing loop

SYNOPSIS
    break

DESCRIPTION
    Zero-argument shell keyword that immediately terminates the nearest
    enclosing for(1), while(1), or until loop. Outside any loop, break
    succeeds as a no-op.

    Because break is parsed as a language keyword before command lookup,
    breakpoints are managed by bp(1) rather than break.

EXAMPLES
    for i in 1 2 3 4; do
        if [ "$i" -eq 3 ]; then break; fi
        echo $i
    done

EXIT STATUS
    0   Always succeeds.

SEE ALSO
    continue(1), for(1), while(1), bp(1)
